(4620001, 662337, 92217, '<td valign="top">very Bresson. I love it.</td>', 'very Bresson. I love it.', '2008-04-07 02:33:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4620013, 663789, 68035, '<td valign="top">Im sure its just my schoolboy sense of humour but your title made me giggle and snort out loud<br/>Brilliant macro and the capture of those antennae is breathtaking<br/> <br/>I really think this was underrated.<br/> <br/>Wonderful counterpoint between the darkness of the butterfly and the brilliance of colours of the flower<br/> <br/><i>Edited for early morning spelling</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-07 01:53:35.</i></td>', 'Im sure its just my schoolboy sense of humour but your title made me giggle and snort out loudBrilliant macro and the capture of those antennae is breathtaking I really think this was underrated. Wonderful counterpoint between the darkness of the butterfly and the brilliance of colours of the flower Edited for early morning spelling', '2008-04-07 02:52:45.000000', '2008-04-07 02:53:35.000000', 0),
(4620016, 662966, 68035, '<td valign="top">For the life of me I cant understand how anyone gave this a 1, 2 or 3.  Even if they dont like they subject then surely the technical strength warrants higher<br/> <br/>I love this shot for the challenge, beautiful curves abound and the slight disorientation between metal and the shadow is cool.  May have prefered it without the cut off but still a lovely image</td>', 'For the life of me I cant understand how anyone gave this a 1, 2 or 3.  Even if they dont like they subject then surely the technical strength warrants higher I love this shot for the challenge, beautiful curves abound and the slight disorientation between metal and the shadow is cool.  May have prefered it without the cut off but still a lovely image', '2008-04-07 02:59:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4620017, 662877, 68035, '<td valign="top">Just think how high this would have scored if you had gone with my title suggestion!!!!<br/> <br/>Well you know how great I think this shot is as has been mentioned it has a fantastic aged look and I think that the crop is perfect<br/> <br/>Wonderful sharpness and great B&amp;W conversion<br/> <br/>Many congrats on the new front page image (even if it does mean that my leave kicking foot is now consigned to the dustbin of history)<br/> <br/>Top top job that makes me smile</td>', 'Just think how high this would have scored if you had gone with my title suggestion!!!! Well you know how great I think this shot is as has been mentioned it has a fantastic aged look and I think that the crop is perfect Wonderful sharpness and great B&W conversion Many congrats on the new front page image (even if it does mean that my leave kicking foot is now consigned to the dustbin of history) Top top job that makes me smile', '2008-04-07 03:02:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4620026, 663564, 67145, '<td valign="top">when i first opened this i thought .. ''wottha??'' .. <br/>i then read the other comments and had another look .. <br/>obviously the voters didnt give this the time it deserved .. coz the more i look the better it gets ...!!!!!<br/>i love the process and the interesting angles .. i still havent worked out wot it is, unless its a swan on its side ... but often not knowing doesnt hurt at all .. it happens to me all the time .. !!!!!!!..<br/>lots of exclamations eh .. ??!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</td>', 'when i first opened this i thought .. ''wottha??'' .. i then read the other comments and had another look .. obviously the voters didnt give this the time it deserved .. coz the more i look the better it gets ...!!!!!i love the process and the interesting angles .. i still havent worked out wot it is, unless its a swan on its side ... but often not knowing doesnt hurt at all .. it happens to me all the time .. !!!!!!!..lots of exclamations eh .. ??!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!', '2008-04-07 03:09:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4620028, 662559, 68035, '<td valign="top">OK, well lets look at the facts before I say anything<br/> <br/>You - 44th 6.1824<br/>Me - 193rd 4.6467<br/> <br/>OK so now having established my credentials, I gotta say that whilst I really like this shot compositionally (but do prefer the outtake) there seems to be something just a little off about it<br/> <br/>I think it make be the dome and the sky which just seem a little fuzzy but for some reason attract my eye more than they should and means I dont get to concerntrate on the beautiful sharpness, texture and repetitive pattern of the arches (which are by the way magnificent)<br/> <br/></td>', 'OK, well lets look at the facts before I say anything You - 44th 6.1824Me - 193rd 4.6467 OK so now having established my credentials, I gotta say that whilst I really like this shot compositionally (but do prefer the outtake) there seems to be something just a little off about it I think it make be the dome and the sky which just seem a little fuzzy but for some reason attract my eye more than they should and means I dont get to concerntrate on the beautiful sharpness, texture and repetitive pattern of the arches (which are by the way magnificent) ', '2008-04-07 03:09:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4620035, 663852, 68035, '<td valign="top">Woohoooooooooooooooooooooooooo!<br/> <br/>C O N G R A T U L A T I O N S on your new highest scoring picture and on the fantastic placement and richly deserved it is to<br/> <br/>A fantastically strong composition and the rich darkness of the bridge counterpoints beautifully with the car lights of the vehicles streaming across it<br/> <br/>Love the fact that the water and the sky are almost the same tone which adds a sense of mirrored symettry<br/> <br/>Fantastic photo - You''re obviously going to become an HDR master if this is only your second effort at it</td>', 'Woohoooooooooooooooooooooooooo! C O N G R A T U L A T I O N S on your new highest scoring picture and on the fantastic placement and richly deserved it is to A fantastically strong composition and the rich darkness of the bridge counterpoints beautifully with the car lights of the vehicles streaming across it Love the fact that the water and the sky are almost the same tone which adds a sense of mirrored symettry Fantastic photo - You''re obviously going to become an HDR master if this is only your second effort at it', '2008-04-07 03:14:22.000000', NULL, 0),
